#!/usr/bin/env python3
# redinstaller-gui: the graphical version of redinstaller. Installs a game's
# Windows redistributables (.exe/.msi, e.g. the _CommonRedist folder) into its
# Steam Proton prefix with Protontricks.
# https://github.com/Jecobe/redinstaller
#
# Needs:  Python 3.8+, GTK 4.10+, libadwaita 1.5+ and PyGObject, plus
#         protontricks (native or Flatpak).
#           Arch:    sudo pacman -S python-gobject gtk4 libadwaita protontricks
#           Debian:  sudo apt install python3-gi gir1.2-gtk-4.0 gir1.2-adw-1
#           Ubuntu:  sudo apt install python3-gi gir1.2-gtk-4.0 gir1.2-adw-1 protontricks
#           Fedora:  sudo dnf install python3-gobject gtk4 libadwaita protontricks
#
# It works like the redinstaller command and shares its settings file
# (~/.config/redinstaller/config, or $REDINSTALLER_CONFIG): pick a game, pick
# the _CommonRedist-style folder (found for you, browsed, or typed), review,
# install. It can also set the game's Steam launch options.
#
# Usage:  redinstaller-gui [options] [FOLDER]
#   --appid ID     preselect a game
#   --recursive    include installers in sub-folders     (--no-recursive)
#   --silent       add quiet flags for known installers   (--no-silent)
#   --flatpak      force Flatpak Protontricks      --native   force native
#   --verbose      keep Wine debug output          --dry-run  print commands only
#   -y, --yes      skip the review screen when nothing needs asking
#   --launch-options[=OPTS]   also set the game's Steam launch options
#   --replace-launch-options  replace existing launch options instead of merging
#   --no-launch-options       don't set launch options this time
#   --no-config    ignore the settings file for this run
#   --version      print the version                -h, --help  this help
